{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggwSidWCQqvr2QoUcitz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For d³ octahedral, ⁴A₂→⁴T₂ = 10Dq, so Dq = 2660 cm⁻¹ (taking 26 600 as ν1).\n\nThe ⁴T₁(F) band is ν2 = 32 500. The Tanabe–Sugano matrix for ⁴T₁ gives:\n\nE(⁴T₁) = 15B + 15Dq − ½[(...)] ... I'll use the standard form instead:\nν2 = 7.5B + 15Dq − ½√((15B − 5Dq)² + 40·B·Dq·... )\n\nThe standard result is ν2 = 15Dq + 7.5B − ½(225B² + 100Dq² − 180B·Dq)^½. It follows that ν3 = 15Dq + 7.5B + ½(...)^½. Adding gives ν2 + ν3 = 30Dq + 15B, and ν3 − ν2 = √(...).\n\nOnly ν1 and ν2 are given, so I solve for B from ν2.\n\nLet x = Dq = 2660. Then 15Dq = 39 900, and ν2 = 32 500.\n39 900 + 7.5B − 32 500 = ½√(225B² + 100x² − 180Bx)\n7400 + 7.5B = ½√(...)\n(14 800 + 15B)² = 225B² + 100x² − 180Bx\n\nLeft side: 219 040 000 + 444 000B + 225B².\nRight side: 225B² + 707 560 000 − 478 800B.\nThe 225B² terms cancel, so 922 800B = 488 520 000 and B = 529.4.\n\nThis B is low, but it is plausible for Cr(CN)6³⁻ (B ≈ 530).\n\nNext, C comes from the ²E energy. To first order, E(²E) ≈ 9B + 3C − 90B²/(10Dq) (a common approximation). This is what I'll use:\n- 9B = 4765\n- 90B²/(10Dq) = 90·280 276/26 600 = 948.4\n- 12 820 = 4765 + 3C − 948 → 3C = 9003, so C ≈ 3001\n\nC/B ≈ 5.7, which is high, but it follows from the data with this approximation.\n\n**Results:** Dq ≈ 2660 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 529 cm⁻¹, C ≈ 3000 cm⁻¹. C depends on the approximate ²E expression, so treat it as less certain than Dq and B.\n\n{\"Dq\": 2660, \"B\": 529, \"C\": 3000, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from ν1, B from the ⁴T₁ energy via the d³ secular equation, C from the approximate ²E expression.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1670,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1670,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"se